`_request` in this same PR gained a `project` parameter, so this method re-implements what already exists one screen below:

```dart
Future<String> getInProject(String project, String path) async {
  final response = await dio.get<String>(
    buildProjectUrl(project, path),
    queryParameters: {'api-version': apiVersion},
    options: Options(headers: headers),
  );
  return response.data ?? '';
}
```

is equivalent to:

```dart
Future<String> getInProject(String project, String path) =>
    _request('GET', path, project: project);
```

(only difference: the extra default `Content-Type: application/json` header on a GET, which is harmless). Keeping one code path means error handling / header assembly stays consistent if `_request` evolves — same argument that motivated extracting `sync_binary_upload.dart` for the curl uploads.
